<p>
Solvetri.c is compiled to the mex file with the options as indicated.=20
The mex file for the matrc routine improves computation time by a factor
 of 2 (more for longer range computations) or so.
</p><p>
Benchmarks in practice... Calculating PE predictions for an acoustic=20
path in the Philippine Sea for 36 ECCO2 ocean model realizations. Time=20
listed is for a single frequency. All values "under load", that is, all=20
cpu's running. Using the 80 cpus of aogreef, the 36 snapshots at 628 km=20
range took about 10 hours total (72sX13 frequencies for each cpuX36=20
realizations=3D9.4 hrs.) All calculations used the mex files compiled with
 the GNU gcc. It appears that the Intel icc compiler might gain an=20
additional 7% or so. compiler with "-fast" option.
