			<td bgcolor=3D"#ffffff" valign=3D"top">
 Comparison between Eigenray prediction and RAM prediction for 1401.745=20
km range. This comparison shows the effects of bathymetry in the form of
 a sharp ridge midway along the acoustic path. The comparison
illustrates two problems that can be fixed by adjustment of the=20
calculation parameters. (1) Note that the ray and PE predictions shown
here have slightly different dispersal, which is particularly evident in
 the early part of the timefront. This is the result of using too large a
 value for "deltaz". When deltaz=3D0.5, rather than 2.0 (as was used=20
here), this discrepancy is resolved. (2) The odd arrival in the lower=20
right hand corner of the PE prediction is a result of using too small a=20
value for T - the window is not wide enough so the earliest arrival=20
appears to overlap the final=E9. A larger value for T will give a window=20
wide enough to encompass the complete arrival pattern with no wrapping=20
around. </td>
